; `:walk-opaque true` says the surrounding schema does not interpret
; this slot's contents, and the defaults overlay stops there with the
; validator's tree walk.
;
; `(circle)` sits in the opaque `:body` slot, so its `:radius` is never
; materialized — and the `(nope)` default that would fail at runtime is
; never evaluated, so no `default_eval_failed` is reported. Compare
; `default-materialize-expression-failure`, the same schema key in a
; slot the schema does read.
;
; Before the overlay honoured `:walk-opaque`, this document reported
; that failure against a slot nothing was going to materialize.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (expr-func :name nope :arity (fixed 0) :result number)
  (form :name host
    (key :name body :type any :walk-opaque true :optional true))
  (form :name circle
    (key :name radius :type number :default (nope))))

(host :body (circle))
